{"content_hash": "94c7ec5d9fa8a05a", "version_id": 208, "article_id": 21, "level_code": "ja_n3", "lang": "ja", "level": 3, "level_label": "N3 中級", "title": "立ち退きが全国の抗議を呼んだスペインの高齢女性が亡くなる", "title_zh": "被赶出家门引发全国抗议的西班牙老人去世了", "topic": "world", "source": "bbc_world", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6e3x21ev9wwo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/240/cpsprodpb/d9ee/live/06010330-c283-11f1-98ea-35e6bf307fc9.jpg", "credit": ""}, "published_date": "2026-10-08", "word_count": 478, "reading_minutes": 1.5, "lead": "スペインのマドリードで、家を追い出された87歳の女性が亡くなりました。この事件をきっかけに、住宅問題について全国で大きな抗議が起きていました。", "lead_zh": "西班牙马德里一位被赶出家的87岁女性去世了。这件事引发了全国范围内针对住房问题的大规模抗议。", "preview": "マドリードのテナント組合によると、マリカルメン・アバスカルさん（87）が亡くなりました。彼女は9月23日、家賃が上がって払えなくなったので、70年以上住んでいたアパートから強制的に出されました。そのとき、彼女はストレッチャーで運ばれました。", "preview_zh": "据马德里租户联盟称，玛丽卡门·阿瓦斯卡尔女士（87岁）去世了。9月23日，因为房租上涨付不起，她被强行从住了70多年的公寓里赶了出来。当时她是被担架抬走的。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 198, "url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@e099b16/content/audio/21/ja_n3.mp3", "duration": 103.25, "size_bytes": 623232, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "ja-JP-NanamiNeural", "word_count": 320, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@e099b16/content/data/versions/208.json", "paragraphs": ["マドリードのテナント組合によると、マリカルメン・アバスカルさん（87）が亡くなりました。彼女は9月23日、家賃が上がって払えなくなったので、70年以上住んでいたアパートから強制的に出されました。そのとき、彼女はストレッチャーで運ばれました。", "アパートを持っていた会社は、その後、もっと安い家賃で戻ってもいいと言いました。しかし、彼女は病院に入院していたので、契約にサインできませんでした。組合は「彼女の状況はこの国の歴史の転換点になった」と話しました。", "彼女の死は、マドリードのプエルタ・デル・ソル広場で大きな驚きとともに受け止められました。人々はろうそくをともし、彼女に祈りをささげました。そして「戦いは続く」「マリ・カルメンは生きている」と叫びながら、国会に向かってデモを行いました。", "アバスカルさんは、スペインの住宅危機のシンボルになりました。父親が1956年から借りていて、彼女が引き継ぎました。しかし、2018年に家を買った会社が、家賃を月500ユーロから2650ユーロに上げました。", "この問題で、政府は緊急の住宅法案を出しましたが、先週議会で否決されました。そのため、週末には全国の都市で数万人が抗議しました。サンチェス首相は11月29日に総選挙を行うと発表しました。"], "paragraphs_zh": ["据马德里租户联盟称，玛丽卡门·阿瓦斯卡尔女士（87岁）去世了。9月23日，因为房租上涨付不起，她被强行从住了70多年的公寓里赶了出来。当时她是被担架抬走的。", "公寓所属的公司后来表示，可以让她以更低的租金搬回去。但是，她因为住院，无法签署协议。联盟表示：“她的情况成了这个国家历史的转折点。”", "她的死讯在马德里太阳门广场引起了巨大的震惊。人们点燃蜡烛，为她祈祷。然后高喊着“斗争将继续”“玛丽·卡门还活着”，向国会方向游行。", "阿瓦斯卡尔女士成了西班牙住房危机的象征。她的父亲从1956年起租住这里，她后来继承了租约。但是，2018年买下这栋房子的公司把月租从500欧元涨到了2650欧元。", "由于这个问题，政府提出了紧急住房法案，但上周在议会遭到否决。因此，周末全国多个城市有数万人抗议。桑切斯首相宣布将于11月29日举行大选。"], "body": "マドリードのテナント組合によると、マリカルメン・アバスカルさん（87）が亡くなりました。彼女は9月23日、家賃が上がって払えなくなったので、70年以上住んでいたアパートから強制的に出されました。そのとき、彼女はストレッチャーで運ばれました。\n\nアパートを持っていた会社は、その後、もっと安い家賃で戻ってもいいと言いました。しかし、彼女は病院に入院していたので、契約にサインできませんでした。組合は「彼女の状況はこの国の歴史の転換点になった」と話しました。\n\n彼女の死は、マドリードのプエルタ・デル・ソル広場で大きな驚きとともに受け止められました。人々はろうそくをともし、彼女に祈りをささげました。そして「戦いは続く」「マリ・カルメンは生きている」と叫びながら、国会に向かってデモを行いました。\n\nアバスカルさんは、スペインの住宅危機のシンボルになりました。父親が1956年から借りていて、彼女が引き継ぎました。しかし、2018年に家を買った会社が、家賃を月500ユーロから2650ユーロに上げました。\n\nこの問題で、政府は緊急の住宅法案を出しましたが、先週議会で否決されました。そのため、週末には全国の都市で数万人が抗議しました。サンチェス首相は11月29日に総選挙を行うと発表しました。", "body_zh": "据马德里租户联盟称，玛丽卡门·阿瓦斯卡尔女士（87岁）去世了。9月23日，因为房租上涨付不起，她被强行从住了70多年的公寓里赶了出来。当时她是被担架抬走的。\n\n公寓所属的公司后来表示，可以让她以更低的租金搬回去。但是，她因为住院，无法签署协议。联盟表示：“她的情况成了这个国家历史的转折点。”\n\n她的死讯在马德里太阳门广场引起了巨大的震惊。人们点燃蜡烛，为她祈祷。然后高喊着“斗争将继续”“玛丽·卡门还活着”，向国会方向游行。\n\n阿瓦斯卡尔女士成了西班牙住房危机的象征。她的父亲从1956年起租住这里，她后来继承了租约。但是，2018年买下这栋房子的公司把月租从500欧元涨到了2650欧元。\n\n由于这个问题，政府提出了紧急住房法案，但上周在议会遭到否决。因此，周末全国多个城市有数万人抗议。桑切斯首相宣布将于11月29日举行大选。", "text": "マドリードのテナント組合によると、マリカルメン・アバスカルさん（87）が亡くなりました。彼女は9月23日、家賃が上がって払えなくなったので、70年以上住んでいたアパートから強制的に出されました。そのとき、彼女はストレッチャーで運ばれました。 アパートを持っていた会社は、その後、もっと安い家賃で戻ってもいいと言いました。しかし、彼女は病院に入院していたので、契約にサインできませんでした。組合は「彼女の状況はこの国の歴史の転換点になった」と話しました。 彼女の死は、マドリードのプエルタ・デル・ソル広場で大きな驚きとともに受け止められました。人々はろうそくをともし、彼女に祈りをささげました。そして「戦いは続く」「マリ・カルメンは生きている」と叫びながら、国会に向かってデモを行いました。 アバスカルさんは、スペインの住宅危機のシンボルになりました。父親が1956年から借りていて、彼女が引き継ぎました。しかし、2018年に家を買った会社が、家賃を月500ユーロから2650ユーロに上げました。 この問題で、政府は緊急の住宅法案を出しましたが、先週議会で否決されました。そのため、週末には全国の都市で数万人が抗議しました。サンチェス首相は11月29日に総選挙を行うと発表しました。", "vocab": [{"word": "立ち退き", "pos": "noun", "zh": "搬迁，驱逐", "note": "被强制离开住处"}, {"word": "家賃", "pos": "noun", "zh": "房租", "note": ""}, {"word": "強制的に", "pos": "adv", "zh": "强制地", "note": "副词形式"}, {"word": "アパート", "pos": "noun", "zh": "公寓", "note": ""}, {"word": "組合", "pos": "noun", "zh": "工会，联盟", "note": "这里指租户联盟"}, {"word": "入院", "pos": "noun/verb", "zh": "住院", "note": "する动词"}, {"word": "抗議", "pos": "noun/verb", "zh": "抗议", "note": ""}, {"word": "ろうそく", "pos": "noun", "zh": "蜡烛", "note": ""}, {"word": "デモ", "pos": "noun", "zh": "游行，示威", "note": ""}, {"word": "危機", "pos": "noun", "zh": "危机", "note": ""}, {"word": "法案", "pos": "noun", "zh": "法案", "note": ""}, {"word": "総選挙", "pos": "noun", "zh": "大选，总选举", "note": ""}], "title_original": "Spanish pensioner whose eviction sparked nationwide protests dies, union says", "summary_original": "Maricarmen Abascal, 87, was forcibly removed on a stretcher from her apartment of more than 70 years in September.", "body_original": "Spanish pensioner whose eviction sparked nationwide protests dies, union says\nBy\nAlys Davies\nand\nAlba Morgade in Madrid\nPublished\n7 October 2026\nUpdated 59 minutes ago\nAn elderly woman whose eviction sparked nationwide protests over Spain's housing crisis and a political row that triggered early elections has died, according to Madrid's tenants union.\nMaricarmen Abascal, 87, was forcibly removed on a stretcher from her apartment of more than 70 years on 23 September after she was unable to afford rent increases.\nThe company that owned the flat later offered to allow her to return at a lower rate - but she was unable to sign an agreement as she had been admitted to hospital.\n\"We regret to announce that Maricarmen passed away today,\" the Madrid Tenants' Union said in a statement, adding her situation marked \"a turning point in the history of this country\".\nUnion spokesperson Alicia del Río said: \"Speculation costs lives, and today rentierism has finished killing our colleague Maricarmen\" but \"her memory lives on with us\".\nA cause of death was not announced.\nAbascal's death was received in Puerta del Sol with a big collective gasp, then followed by a minute of silence.\nIt is in this square in the centre of Madrid where thousands have been camping since Abascal's eviction last month to demand more affordable housing.\nOn Wednesday, it became the place to pay tribute to her.\nPeople lit dozens of candles around the square in a small improvised vigil that glowed with a warm light on a dry and warm autumn night.\nOther candles formed an altar to Abascal in front of the headquarters of the Community of Madrid government.\nMessages on cardboard banners next to the candles read \"it's not a death, it's a killing\", \"the fight will continue\" and \"Mari Carmen, the grandmother of the whole country\", among others.\nA few hundred people then took to the streets that connect Puerta del Sol with the Spanish Congress, just 500m away, in an improvised protest.\nDuring the march people chanted: \"We will not tolerate a single eviction more\" and \"the fight will continue, Mari Carmen is still alive\". There were other chants against fascism and against the police.\nThe police had set up barriers to block the march. There was not a big police presence, and there was the tension that protests sometimes have.\nMany protesters seemed to feel the police have been complicit in the evictions, as under court orders they have to remove tenants who have been served eviction notices.\nAfter a couple of hours, the chants near Congress gave way to another minute of silence. Then, a big collective shout of \"murderers\".\nWednesday night's march has finished, but the camping, already on its 12th night, will continue \"as long as necessary\" one of the protesters told the BBC.\nAbascal became a symbol for Spain's housing crisis following her eviction.\nHer father first rented the property in 1956 and she continued as the tenant after her parents died, during which time there was a cap on the rent.\nHowever, Urbagestión, which bought the property in 2018, increased the rent from €500 per month (£428; $572) to €2,650 (£2,280; $3,020).\nThe company later offered to reduce this to €1,650 - still €300 more than Abascal's monthly pension.\nThree previous attempts to evict her were blocked by the courts and the case has received increasing media attention.\nAnger over the situation grew, leading to protests and putting pressure on the coalition government to approve emergency housing legislation -\nbut it was rejected in Congress last week\n.\nThat led to further protests,\nwith tens of thousands of people taking\nto the streets\nin cities across the country over the weekend.\nReferring to the rejected bills, the Madrid Tenants' Union said: \"While a historic agreement was reached that would have allowed her to return to her home, this solution has come too late. An absolutely avoidable situation after a torturing process.\"\nIt said the events surrounding her eviction represented a turning point in the country's history, but added that the cost to get to this point had been \"too high\".\n\"Above all, we will fulfil what she always asked of us: 'fight, keep fighting for what is yours',\" it said.\nIn a video recorded from her hospital bed following her eviction, Maricarmen said: \"I haven't managed to defend my home, but I have fought so that others can learn to fight for what's theirs.\"\n\"All my love goes to Maricarmen's family and loved ones,\" Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sánchez said. \"A hug as well to everyone who today feels this loss as their own.\"\nOpposition People's Party leader Alberto Núñez Feijóo also sent his condolences to Maricarmen's loved ones, as he said on X: \"No campaign, no parties, no self-interested exploitation. No more stones in the wall.\n\"In the face of a person's death, only respect is in order,\" he added.\nEarlier on Wednesday, unions had called a general strike to take place on 11 November, demanding housing reforms.\nThe public outcry over Abascal's situation has led to political turmoil in Spain.\nOn Monday Sánchez, who leads a leftist coalition that does not hold a majority in parliament, called an early election for 29 November. It followed his failure to get the emergency housing legislation through Congress.\nThe political right had argued that the government's attempt to intervene in the housing market would have led to fewer homes being rented and would have raised prices further.\nSpeaking on Monday, Sánchez said he needed \"a broader progressive majority\" that can \"overcome the resistance of the elites\" to push through reforms.\nOther issues not relating to housing, such as numerous corruption scandals linked to his party, and pressures relating to the cost of living and immigration, have also caused him problems.\nMost opinion polls suggest the conservatives are likely to emerge as the largest party in the next election. However, they would be expected to need the support of the hard-right Vox party to form a government.\nAdditional reporting by Tom McArthur\nRelated topics\nSpain\nMore on this story\nSpanish PM Sánchez calls early election after housing protests\nPublished\n2 days ago\nDramatic eviction of woman aged 87 highlights Spain's housing shortage\nPublished\n23 September", "fetched_at": "2026-10-08T01:16:22.071120+00:00", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "マドリード", "s": 0.125, "e": 0.725, "sm": 125, "em": 725, "cs": 0, "ce": 5, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "の", "s": 0.738, "e": 0.863, "sm": 737, "em": 862, "cs": 5, "ce": 6, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "テナント", "s": 0.875, "e": 1.35, "sm": 875, "em": 1350, "cs": 6, "ce": 10, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "組合", "s": 1.363, "e": 1.812, "sm": 1362, "em": 1812, "cs": 10, "ce": 12, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "に", "s": 1.825, "e": 1.925, "sm": 1825, "em": 1925, "cs": 12, "ce": 13, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "よる", "s": 1.938, "e": 2.163, "sm": 1937, "em": 2162, "cs": 13, "ce": 15, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "と", "s": 2.175, "e": 2.375, "sm": 2175, "em": 2375, "cs": 15, "ce": 16, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "、", "s": 2.375, "e": 2.712, "sm": 2375, "em": 2712, "cs": 16, "ce": 17, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "マリカルメ